Subject: retain DHI security resolutions after Kibana pnpm migration
Origin: DHI-internal (package security overrides)
Description: Apply DHI-maintained pnpm resolutions in package.json and
 pnpm-workspace.yaml so bootstrap keeps CVE-fixed dependency versions and
 the Elastic kibana-d3-color fork across nested pnpm layouts after upstream's
 pnpm migration. The kibana-d3-color fork is not applied with an unscoped
 "**/d3-color" resolution: that selector replaces d3-color 3.x with the 2.0.1
 fork, and d3-interpolate@3, d3-scale-chromatic@3, d3-transition@3, and vega
 depend on d3-color 3. Upstream's "**/d3-scale/**/d3-color" resolution and
 scoped d3-interpolate@2.0.1 override are left as-is. The zod override is
 scoped to zod@>=4.0.0, matching Kibana's own 4.x pin, and does not rewrite
 zod 3.x.
Base-Tree: git https://github.com/elastic/kibana 29f3bc23ca2701e6db5e0b8929e799bddcba0443 path=package.json
Verify: cmd `patch -p1 --dry-run -i package/main/kibana/patch/pnpm-security-overrides_9.4.patch` expect "checking file pnpm-workspace.yaml"
Forwarded: not-needed (DHI-maintained resolution pins until upstream absorbs them)
Drop-When: never: delete only after upstream v9.4.x carries equivalent or newer CVE-fixed pnpm resolutions without these hunks

